<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-AL CAPONE II WINS GRAND STEEPLE-CHASE DE PARIS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-AL CAPONE II WINS GRAND STEEPLE-CHASE DE PARIS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Grand Steeple-Chase de Paris for five-years-olds and up run over three miles and five furlongs (5.8 kms) at Auteuil on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Al Capone II (Jean-Yves Beaurain)</p>
<p>2. Cand d'Or (Franck Smeulders)</p>
<p>3. Gracky (Patrice Julien)</p>
<p>4. Chamberko (Christophe Pieux)</p>
<p>Six ran.</p>
<p>Distances: 10 lengths, 4 lengths, 1-1/2 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Robert Fougedoire, trained by Bernard Secly (France).</p>
<p>Value to the winner: $226,262. Pari-Mutuel (inc one-franc stake): win 1.50 (coupled with Baccarat Collonges and Cumberland); places 1.30, 3.40. Straight forecast 25.90.</p>
</text>
